# Gather typosquat from vendor APIs

This path is **separate** from dnstwist-driven typosquat detection (see [`typosquat-detection.mdc`](typosquat-detection.mdc)). It pulls domains from **ThreatStream** and **Recorded Future** and posts them to the API as typosquat findings.

## Entry points and layout

| Piece | Role |
|-------|------|
| [`src/runner/app/batch_jobs/gather_api_findings.py`](src/runner/app/batch_jobs/gather_api_findings.py) | `GatherApiFindingsTask`: credentials, dedupe, batch create/update, cross-enrichment orchestration |
| [`src/runner/app/batch_jobs/api_vendors/base.py`](src/runner/app/batch_jobs/api_vendors/base.py) | `BaseAPIVendor`: `gather_domains`, `create_finding_data`, credential validation |
| [`src/runner/app/batch_jobs/api_vendors/threatstream.py`](src/runner/app/batch_jobs/api_vendors/threatstream.py) | TS: `q=` list gather; `fetch_intelligence_by_value` for `?value=` enrichment |
| [`src/runner/app/batch_jobs/api_vendors/recordedfuture.py`](src/runner/app/batch_jobs/api_vendors/recordedfuture.py) | RF: alert search + `domain_abuse` details; `fetch_enrichment_for_domain` (entity search + details with `ignore_status_filter=True`) |
| [`src/runner/app/batch_jobs/api_vendors/config.py`](src/runner/app/batch_jobs/api_vendors/config.py) | Runtime query/retry overrides via env |
| [`src/runner/app/batch_jobs/refresh_vendor_intel.py`](src/runner/app/batch_jobs/refresh_vendor_intel.py) | `RefreshVendorIntelTask`: data-only refresh for findings that already have vendor JSONB |

**ThreatStream list gather** (`gather_domains`, the paginated `q=` intelligence search) requires a non-empty **`custom_query`** from job payload (`job_data.custom_query` for scheduled jobs). Vendor config does not supply a default feed/itype/pattern query; pagination limits still come from [`config.py`](src/runner/app/batch_jobs/api_vendors/config.py) / env.

Register new vendors in `GatherApiFindingsTask._create_vendor_adapter` and implement the base class.

## Credentials

- Primary vendor: `get_program_api_credentials` → GET `/programs/{name}` mapped via `adapter.get_credential_fields()`.
- Other vendor (cross-enrichment): `_get_vendor_credentials(program_name, "threatstream" \| "recordedfuture")`. If incomplete, skip enrichment; do not fail the job.

## Finding shape and API

- Per domain: `vendor_adapter.create_finding_data(domain_data, program_name)` produces `{typo_domain, program_name, source, ...}` plus `{vendor}_data` JSONB payload.
- **Batch create**: POST `{api_base}/findings/typosquat` with top-level **`program_id`** (UUID) and optional `program_name`; body wraps `findings.typosquat_domain[]`. Scheduled `gather_api_findings` jobs receive `program_id` from the schedule row (`program_ids[0]`) in the K8s ConfigMap; if missing (older payloads), the task falls back to GET `/programs/{name}`.
- **Patches** (updates / enrichment): `PATCH .../typosquat/{id}/recordedfuture-data`, `PATCH .../threatstream-data`, `PATCH .../recordedfuture-derived-columns` (API routes under `/findings`).

WHOIS-related fields in create/update payloads are stored on **`typosquat_apex_domains`** (registrable domain per program); API responses merge those fields onto each finding as flat `whois_*` keys.

## Cross-vendor enrichment (best-effort)

After `create_finding_data`, `_enrich_single_finding_cross_vendor` merges the **other** vendor when credentials exist:

- **RF-primary** → TS: `GET https://api.threatstream.com/api/v2/intelligence/?value={domain}` → `threatstream_data`.
- **TS-primary** → RF: `POST .../playbook-alert/search` with `entity: ["idn:{domain}"]`, pick alert, then existing **`_fetch_alert_details(..., ignore_status_filter=True)`** → `build_recordedfuture_vendor_blob` → **`recordedfuture_data` only** on the finding (no extra root columns from RF on the batch payload).

## Recorded Future playbook mutations (strict)

**Mutate RF playbook** (e.g. `PUT .../playbook-alert/common/{id}` unassign) **only** when the job is **Recorded Future–primary** (`self.api_vendor == "recordedfuture"`), e.g. `_resolve_recordedfuture_assignees`, `_resolve_filtered_rf_alerts`, `_update_recordedfuture_finding` unassign path.

When **only** enriching from RF (ThreatStream-primary job):

- Do **not** call assignee resolution / RF uhash → `assigned_to` mapping for that enrichment.
- Do **not** PUT/unassign or otherwise update the playbook for enrichment-only data.
- Persist **only** `recordedfuture_data` (and internal API patches limited to that for TS update path).

Read-only RF use for enrichment (search, details GET/POST, screenshot **fetch**) is allowed; avoid alert state **writes** unless primary source is RF.

## Operational notes

- Reuse shared `aiohttp` session from `_get_session()` for volume and TLS reuse.
- RF pre-flight filter + filtered-alert resolve run only for **recordedfuture** vendor on **new** domains.
- Post-storage screenshots: `_handle_recordedfuture_post_storage` uses RF token from `_get_vendor_credentials(..., "recordedfuture")` and `RecordedFutureAdapter.process_post_storage_tasks` for findings with `raw_details`. The gather task passes resolved **`program_id`** into that path; RF post-storage **`POST /findings/typosquat-url`** and **`POST /findings/typosquat-screenshot`** both require it (same as domain batch create).

When extending behavior, keep **primary vendor** vs **enrichment-only** semantics explicit so RF customer alerts are never modified by TS-led jobs.

## Refresh vendor intel (`refresh_vendor_intel`)

Use this job to **re-fetch vendor JSONB** on **existing** typosquat findings without changing workflow state.

| Piece | Role |
|-------|------|
| [`src/runner/app/batch_jobs/refresh_vendor_intel.py`](src/runner/app/batch_jobs/refresh_vendor_intel.py) | `RefreshVendorIntelTask` |
| API | `POST /jobs/refresh-vendor-intel`; scheduled job type `refresh_vendor_intel` |
| Runner | `run_refresh_vendor_intel_job()` in [`run-job.py`](src/runner/app/run-job.py) |

**Selection (not `source=` filter):**

- RF: `POST /findings/typosquat/search` with `has_recordedfuture: true`
- TS: same search with `has_threatstream: true`

**Refresh paths:**

- **RF:** `bulk_fetch_alert_details(..., ignore_status_filter=True)` by stored `alert_id` → `PATCH .../recordedfuture-data` (+ optional `recordedfuture-derived-columns`). Screenshots via `RecordedFutureAdapter.process_post_storage_tasks` when `include_screenshots` is true.
- **TS:** `ThreatStreamAdapter.fetch_intelligence_by_value(domain)` → `PATCH .../threatstream-data`. If finding also has RF `raw_details`, missing RF screenshots may still be downloaded (RF creds required).

**Hard invariants (unlike `sync_recordedfuture_data` and RF-primary gather):**

- Never `PUT .../typosquat/{id}/status` (no status / `assigned_to` changes)
- Never RF playbook `PUT .../playbook-alert/common/{id}`
- Never assignee resolution, unassign, or filter-resolve

**Screenshot skip:** `RecordedFutureAdapter._process_screenshots` lists existing screenshots for the typosquat URL (`POST /findings/typosquat-screenshot/search`) and skips RF images whose `created` timestamp already exists as `source_created_at`.

**Payload (`job_data`):** `api_vendor` (`recordedfuture` \| `threatstream`), `refresh_options`: `batch_size`, `max_age_hours` (skip if `last_fetched` is newer), `include_screenshots` (default true).

Schedule one job per vendor when both RF and TS intel need periodic refresh.
